        "problem": "Find the angle between $a=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 7\\end{aligned}]$ and $b=[\\begin{aligned}6 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$ Round your answer to $1$ decimal place.",
        "worked_solution": "Rearranging the dot product formula, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{|\\,a\\,||\\,b\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}}{\\sqrt{{a}_{x}^{2}+{a}_{y}^{2}}\\sqrt{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot 6+7\\cdot 1}{\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+{7}^{2}}\\sqrt{{6}^{2}+{1}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{\\sqrt{53}\\cdot \\sqrt{37}} \\\\  & =\\frac{19}{\\sqrt{1961}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}⁡(\\frac{19}{\\sqrt{1961}})≈{64.6}^{∘}.\n$$",
